======================================================================
3b. ANALYTICS QUALITY  (the brief asks for 95% precision and 100% clean analytics)
======================================================================
  Composite = share of ALL tickets that end up correctly tagged.
  Auto-routed tickets are tagged at model precision; the rest by first line.
  The first-line rate is an assumption, not a measurement here, so it is swept.

  first line at 75%
    best composite   95.2%  at coverage 89.0%, model precision 97.7%
    full automation  92.2%
    all manual       75.0%
  first line at 85%
    best composite   96.3%  at coverage 88.1%, model precision 97.9%
    full automation  92.2%
    all manual       85.0%
  first line at 95%
    best composite   98.3%  at coverage 78.3%, model precision 99.2%
    full automation  92.2%
    all manual       95.0%

  No operating point reaches 100%. Raising precision past the optimum lowers
  composite quality, because every ticket withheld goes to the less accurate path.

======================================================================
3c. PER-CATEGORY CERTIFICATION  (what a single global threshold hides)
======================================================================
  A global threshold is set by the categories carrying the volume. The long
  tail rides underneath it, auto-routed on a guarantee never established for
  those categories. Certifying each class on its own calibration items removes
  that, and most classes then fail to certify.

  target 95%
    one global threshold : coverage  87.2%  error 0.020
    per category         : coverage  41.9%  error 0.008
    categories certified : 1 of 43 the classifier ever predicts
                           1 of 53 in the taxonomy. The other 10 are never
                           predicted at all, so they cannot be automated either
      certified classes hold 805 calibration items or more
      uncertified classes: median 7 items, largest 440
    minimum calibration items for any class to certify: 317
      (141 without the across-class correction, so sample size binds, not multiplicity)

  target 97%
    one global threshold : coverage  80.1%  error 0.011
    per category         : coverage   0.0%  error nan
    categories certified : 0 of 43 the classifier ever predicts
                           0 of 53 in the taxonomy. The other 10 are never
                           predicted at all, so they cannot be automated either
      uncertified classes: median 8 items, largest 805
    minimum calibration items for any class to certify: 527
      (235 without the across-class correction, so sample size binds, not multiplicity)


